    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d17">

                <pb facs="0074" n="43" xml:id="pg43"/>

                <head>17. Memorandum From Richard Pipes of the National Security Council Staff to
                    the President’s Assistant for National Security Affairs (Clark)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d17-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1982-08-26">August 26,
                    1982</date></dateline></opener>
                <!--<pb facs="d17-2" n="2" type="facsimile" xml:id="d17-2"/>-->
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>NSDD on Eastern Europe</item>
                </list>
                <p>As State and Commerce were unable to agree upon mutually satisfactory language to
                    define our policy on Technology Transfer in the NSDD on Eastern Europe, I
                    recommend that the original text at Tab A be used.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d17-f2"
                    /></p>
                <p>State, Defense and Norman Bailey concur with this decision.<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d17-f3"/></p>
                <p rendition="#section-heading #italic">Recommendation</p>
                <p>That you forward the memorandum at Tab I to the President with the text of the
                        NSDD.<anchor n="4" xml:id="d17-f4"/></p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d17-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d17-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Reagan Library, Executive Secretariat, NSC National Security Decision
                    Directives (NSDD) Files, NSDD 54 9/2/1982. Secret. Sent for action. Copies were
                    sent to Dobriansky and Stearman. “Signed” is stamped at the top of the
                    memorandum.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d17-f2" n="2" xml:id="d17-f2-content">
                <p>Not found attached. See <ref target="#d12">Document 12</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d17-f3" n="3" xml:id="d17-f3-content">
                <p>Bailey initialed his concurrence above his name.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d17-f4" n="4" xml:id="d17-f4-content">
                <p>The “Approve” option was checked. Underneath the recommendations and written in
                    an unknown hand, is the notation “9/1/82 WPC s/memo to Pres. Copy will be
                    Dacom’ed to Pres.” The memorandum to Reagan, who was at his ranch in California
                    August 26–31, was not found attached.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
